---
import './certificate-journey.css';

const icons = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/icons/';
const components = [
  { icon: 'deploy', name: 'Signer', incoming: 'Watch requests', outgoing: 'Signed chain' },
  { icon: 'api', name: 'API server', incoming: 'Create request', outgoing: 'Signed chain' },
  { icon: 'node', name: 'Kubelet', outgoing: 'Key + chain' },
  { icon: 'pod', name: 'Pod' },
];
---
<figure class="issuance-map" aria-labelledby="issuance-caption">
  <figcaption id="issuance-caption">How a pod gets its certificate</figcaption>
  <div class="issuance-rail" aria-hidden="true">
    {components.map(({ icon, name, incoming, outgoing }) => <>
      <div class="issuance-actor">
        <img src={icons + icon + '.svg'} width="56" height="56" alt="" />
        <strong>{name}</strong>
      </div>
      {outgoing && <div class="issuance-links">
        {incoming && <div class="issuance-edge incoming"><span>{incoming}</span><i></i></div>}
        <div class="issuance-edge outgoing">
          <span>
            {icon !== 'node' && <svg viewBox="0 0 20 24" width="15" height="18" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path d="M3 1h9l5 5v13H3z M12 1v6h5 M6 9h5 M6 12h3" />
              <circle cx="13" cy="16" r="3" /><path d="m11 18-1 5 3-2 3 2-1-5"/>
            </svg>}
            {outgoing}
          </span><i></i>
        </div>
      </div>}
    </>)}
  </div>
  <p>Kubelet creates the key and submits a certificate request. The signer watches the API server and writes the signed chain to request status.</p>
  <p>Kubelet reads the chain and mounts it with the local private key in the pod.</p>
</figure>
